This project is a clean-room-style behavioral reimplementation ("clone") of
PuTTY; it is not affiliated with Simon Tatham. PuTTY itself is
copyright 1997-2025 Simon Tatham and distributed under the MIT license.
Reverse-engineering evidence gathered from the shipped PuTTY 0.83 binary
(see docs/REA_EVIDENCE.md) is used descriptively; no upstream C source or
binaries are redistributed here. The PPK sample in
testdata/ppk-v3-ed25519-sample.txt is a well-known public test vector that
ships inside puttygen.exe itself (MIT, Simon Tatham).
